  <section class="section-b operations-excellence" aria-labelledby="ops-heading">
    <div class="ops-bg" aria-hidden="true">
      <picture>
        <source type="image/avif" srcset="/images/infographics/day-to-day-reality.avif 1x, /images/infographics/day-to-day-reality-640w.avif 640w" sizes="100vw" />
        <source type="image/webp" srcset="/images/infographics/day-to-day-reality.webp 1x, /images/infographics/day-to-day-reality-640w.webp 640w" sizes="100vw" />
        <img src="/images/infographics/day-to-day-reality.jpg" srcset="/images/infographics/day-to-day-reality.jpg 1x, /images/infographics/day-to-day-reality-640w.jpg 640w" sizes="100vw" alt="" width="720" height="1280" loading="lazy" />
      </picture>
    </div>

    <div class="ops-inner">
      <div class="ops-header">
        <span class="section-eyebrow ops-eyebrow">Day-to-Day Reality</span>
        <h2 id="ops-heading">What It Takes to Run One</h2>
        <p class="ops-lede">A license is the starting line. The work that decides whether you make it past year two is the daily operations rhythm — inventory, compliance, and customer insight, all running in parallel. Here are the three modules that consume an operator's day, with the costs the licensing guides don't show you.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ops-modules">
        <article class="ops-module" data-module="01">
          <header class="ops-module-header">
            <span class="mod-num">01</span>
            <h3 class="mod-head">Inventory — METRC seed-to-sale</h3>
            <span class="mod-cost">$2,500–$5,000 <em>annual setup</em></span>
          </header>
          <p class="mod-body">Every plant is tagged at planting. Every transfer between cultivation, manufacturing, and retail is logged in <a href="/guides/maine-metrc-compliance-guide">METRC</a> within the required window. Missed tags compound into the citations an OCP inspector will find: written warning → $1,000–$10,000 fine → license suspension. Day-2 cost is the $2,500–$5,000 annual setup plus $0.45 per plant tag and $0.25 per package tag.</p>
          <!-- analytics:cta-injected id=cta-inline-index-06 -->
<a href="/guides/maine-metrc-compliance-guide" class="mod-cta" data-cta-id="cta-inline-index-06">Read the METRC compliance guide →</a>
        </article>

        <article class="ops-module" data-module="02">
          <header class="ops-module-header">
            <span class="mod-num">02</span>
            <h3 class="mod-head">Compliance — OCP comms + 280E tax</h3>
            <span class="mod-cost">$5,000–$25,000 <em>per year</em></span>
          </header>
          <p class="mod-body">Quarterly OCP reports, annual renewals, and the <a href="/guides/maine-cannabis-taxes-2026">280E tax burden</a> that disallows ordinary business deductions. Combined with Maine's 5.5% state sales tax, the effective tax rate "can approach 70%" (Whitney Economics, April 2026). The Jan 1, 2026 tax restructure (P.L. 2025 ch. 388) means operators need separate medical / adult-use P&amp;L. Day-2 cost is the cannabis-specialized CPA.</p>
          <!-- analytics:cta-injected id=cta-inline-index-07 -->
<a href="/guides/maine-cannabis-taxes-2026" class="mod-cta" data-cta-id="cta-inline-index-07">Read the 280E tax guide →</a>
        </article>

        <article class="ops-module" data-module="03">
          <header class="ops-module-header">
            <span class="mod-num">03</span>
            <h3 class="mod-head">Customer insight — budtender training</h3>
            <span class="mod-cost">40–60% <em>industry turnover</em></span>
          </header>
          <p class="mod-body">Maine customers — especially in Portland metro and mid-coast college towns — ask about cultivation method, terpene profile, and COAs before they buy. Operators who keep budtender turnover low (industry: 40–60% annually) invest in weekly product training and paid certification pathways. The "cashier mindset" — budtenders as checkout clerks rather than product experts — is the most common reason a quality-focused shop loses repeat customers.</p>
          <!-- analytics:cta-injected id=cta-inline-index-08 -->
<a href="/guides/maine-cannabis-staffing-licensing" class="mod-cta" data-cta-id="cta-inline-index-08">Read the staffing &amp; licensing guide →</a>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="ops-footer">
        <p class="ops-hero-stat">
          <span class="ops-hero-stat-num">$2.24B</span>
          <span class="ops-hero-stat-label">Federal 280E excess tax paid by U.S. cannabis operators in 2025 alone (Whitney Economics, April 9, 2026).</span>
        </p>

        <p class="ops-closing">
          <strong>Operators who survive past year two share three habits:</strong> meticulous record-keeping, proactive OCP communication, and a genuine interest in what their customers want.
        </p>

        <div class="ops-topics">
          <a href="/guides/maine-metrc-compliance-guide" class="topic-tag">METRC &amp; Inventory</a>
          <a href="/guides/maine-cannabis-taxes-2026" class="topic-tag">280E Tax Strategy</a>
